#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:2
msgid "Visual diff"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:4
msgid ""
"Get a list of documentation files that changed between the :doc:`pull "
"request </pull-requests>` and the latest version of the documentation, and "
"see their differences highlighted visually on the documentation pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:7
msgid ""
"While seeing changes in source files is helpful, it can be difficult to "
"understand how those changes will look in the rendered documentation, or "
"their impact on the documentation as a whole. Read the Docs makes it easy to "
"see the changes in the rendered documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:13
msgid "Show diff menu in preview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:15 ../../../visual-diff.rst:39
msgid "To enable or disable this feature for your project:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:17
msgid ""
"Go to your project's :menuselection:`Settings --> Addons --> Visual diff`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:18
msgid "Check or uncheck the :guilabel:`Visual diff enabled` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:19 ../../../visual-diff.rst:61
msgid "Click on :guilabel:`Save`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:21
msgid ""
"When enabled, a new UI element appears at the top right of the page showing "
"a dropdown selector containing all the files that have changed in that pull "
"request build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:26
msgid ""
"You can select any of those files from the dropdown to jump directly into "
"that page. Once there, you can toggle Visual Diff on and off by pressing "
"the :guilabel:`Show diff` link from the UI element, or pressing the ``d`` "
"key if you have hotkeys enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:29
msgid ""
"Visual diff shows all the sections that have changed, highlighting their "
"differences with red/green background colors. You can jump between each of "
"these chunks by clicking on the up/down arrows."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:33
msgid "Show build overview in pull requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:37
msgid ""
"This feature is only available for projects connected to a :ref:`reference/"
"git-integration:GitHub App`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:41
msgid "Go to your project's :menuselection:`Settings --> Pull request builds`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:42
msgid ""
"Check or uncheck the :guilabel:`Show build overview in a comment` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:43
msgid "Click on :guilabel:`Update`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:45
msgid ""
"When enabled, a comment is added to the pull request when changes are "
"detected between the pull request and the latest version of the "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:50
msgid "General settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:53
msgid "Ignored files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:55
msgid ""
"You can configure a list of files or patterns to be ignored when listing the "
"files that changed in the pull request. This is useful when you have files "
"that have a date in them, or listing/archive files that show changes without "
"content changes in those files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:59
msgid ""
"Go to your project's :menuselection:`Settings --> Addons --> File tree diff`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:60
msgid ""
"In the :guilabel:`Ignored files` field, add one or more patterns to ignore, "
"one per line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:63
msgid ""
"Patterns are matched against the relative paths of the HTML files produced "
"by the build, you should try to match ``index.html``, not ``docs/"
"index.rst``, nor ``/en/latest/index.html``. Patterns can include one or more "
"of the following special characters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:67
msgid "``*`` matches everything, including slashes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:68
msgid "``?`` matches any single character."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:69
msgid "``[seq]`` matches any character in ``seq``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:72
msgid "Base version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:74
msgid ""
"The base version is the version of the documentation that is used to compare "
"against the pull request. By default, this is the ``latest`` version of the "
"documentation. This is useful if your ``latest`` version doesn't point to "
"the default branch of your repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:80
msgid "This option can be changed by contacting :doc:`/support`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:82
msgid ""
"When the first successful build of a pull request runs, Read the Docs takes "
"a snapshot of the base version's current file manifest and pins it as the "
"baseline for that pull request. Subsequent builds of the pull request are "
"compared against this pinned snapshot instead of whatever the base version "
"happens to contain at that moment. This prevents unrelated files from "
"appearing as changed when the base branch moves forward while the pull "
"request is open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:92
msgid "How main content is detected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:94
msgid ""
"The visual diff compares the \"main content\" of HTML pages, ignoring "
"headers, footers, navigation, and other page elements that aren't part of "
"the documentation content itself. This helps avoid false positives, like all "
"pages being marked as changed because of a date or commit hash being updated "
"in the footer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:98
msgid ""
"For details on how the main content area is detected, see :ref:`reference/"
"main-content-detection:detection logic`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:103
msgid ""
"If the heuristic root element picked by Visual Diff is wrong for your "
"project theme, set the :guilabel:`CSS main content selector` in your "
"project's :menuselection:`Settings --> Addons --> Advanced`. Visual Diff "
"honors this override; other features like Server Side Search do not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:106
msgid "Limitations and known issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:108
msgid "The diff considers HTML files only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:109
msgid ""
"The diff is done between the files from the latest successful build of the "
"pull request and the default base version (latest by default). A snapshot of "
"the base version's manifest is saved on the first successful build of the "
"pull request, so the diff stays stable as the base branch moves forward. If "
"the pull request is later updated against a newer base, the snapshot is not "
"currently refreshed automatically, and the diff may show stale differences "
"until this is addressed in a future update."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:112
msgid ""
"Invisible changes. Some sections may be highlighted as changed, even when "
"they haven't actually visually changed. This can happen when the underlying "
"HTML changes without a corresponding visual change, for example, if a link's "
"URL is updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:114
msgid ""
"Tables may be shown to have changes when they have not actually changed. "
"This is due to subtle variations in how HTML tables are rendered, and will "
"be fixed in a future version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../visual-diff.rst:116
msgid ""
"The background of diff chunks may be incorrect when we are unable to detect "
"the correct main parent element for the chunk."
msgstr ""
